  "audio_file": "short_sf_cargo_rules.mp3",
  "text": "The SRE Rules of Slimefun Cargo Logistics:\n1. Avoid feedback loops to stop CPU tree traversal.\n2. Segregate 16 frequency channels by item type.\n3. Use round-robin output nodes to prevent buffer saturation.\nZero-lag engineering on play.drakescraft.cl!",
  "spoken_text": "If you want high-throughput industrial automation without tanking your server ticks, follow these SRE rules for Slimefun cargo. First: avoid closed cargo feedback loops. Items circulating indefinitely consume CPU cycles traversing graph trees. Second: segregate your cargo channels. Slimefun provides sixteen independent frequency channels. Keep channel zero strictly for raw ores, channel one for dusts, and channel two for ingots. Third: connect Cargo Output Nodes directly to auto-crafters with round-robin distribution to prevent buffer saturation. Experience zero-lag industrial engineering right now on play dot drakescraft dot cl.",
